<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Julio-Claudian dynasty</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/27-bce">27 BCE</a> – <a href="/years/68">68 CE</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/1st-century-bce">1st century BCE</a> · Also known as Julio-Claudians</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Julio-Claudian dynasty comprised the first five Roman emperors, Augustus, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tiberius">Tiberius</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caligula">Caligula</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/claudius">Claudius</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nero">Nero</a>, who ruled the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-empire">Roman Empire</a> from its formation under Augustus in 27 BCE until Nero's suicide in 68 CE. The name is a historiographical term joining the two families of the house, the Julii Caesares and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/claudia-gens">Claudii</a> Nerones. Since Augustus, Caligula and Nero had no legitimate biological sons, the emperors used adoption to promote their chosen heirs: Augustus adopted his stepson Tiberius, and Claudius his great-nephew and stepson Nero. Within a year of Nero's death, after a brief civil war, the Flavian emperors succeeded the dynasty.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/julio-claudian-dynasty.jpg" alt="Julio-Claudian dynasty" width="330" height="495" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Till Niermann · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Statue-Augustus.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>His stepson Tiberius succeeded him, confirming the hereditary principle of the <b>Julio-Claudian dynasty</b>.</blockquote><a href="/today-in-history/august-19">19 August in history</a></li><li><blockquote>Adopted by Claudius, he became emperor at 16 and was the last of the <b>Julio-Claudian dynasty</b>.</blockquote><a href="/today-in-history/december-15">15 December in history</a></li><li><blockquote>His death ended the <b>Julio-Claudian dynasty</b> and opened the Year of the Four Emperors.</blockquote><a href="/today-in-history/june-9">9 June in history</a></li></ul></section>
